  "version": "0.7.1-beta.1",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.0`\n\n### Features\n\n- show the macOS icon on a macOS host's SSH tabs: the probe only read /etc/os-release, which macOS lacks, so its tabs got no icon; it now falls back to sw_vers and runs under sh -s, since a csh login shell took its 2>/dev/null for an argument and reported nothing ([ea096fc9](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/ea096fc9d6e41fdc81d59526ef3d5b745b019eee))\n- monitor macOS and FreeBSD hosts, not only Linux: the script now has a section per system and runs under sh -s, so csh and fish login shells work too; FreeBSD reads CPU ticks, memory pages and the ZFS cache from sysctl and swap from swapinfo, while macOS reads memory as Activity Monitor counts it from vm_stat and measures the CPU over one second with iostat, since it keeps no tick counters and top costs almost a second of CPU per sample; both read the default interface's netstat counters and df with mount, where APFS volumes report their container's usage, hidden macOS volumes are skipped and ZFS datasets fold into one row per pool; other systems get a translated message naming them instead of the English-only \"Only Linux hosts are supported\", and FreeBSD and macOS get icons of their own ([e258b797](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e258b7975b12ec01f82687c68d5b1833f9e2658a))\n- duplicate the active tab from the keyboard with Mod+Shift+D: copying a terminal took a trip to its context menu, while renaming and closing already had chords; the new tabs.duplicateActive action follows Windows Terminal's Ctrl+Shift+D, can be rebound or unbound in the keymap settings, shows beside Duplicate Tab in the tab bar's and split group's menus, and lets the chord through on page tabs and remote file editors, which cannot be copied ([9a67a60e](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/9a67a60ef1f382ee57396bef87426d6ce97c7bc1))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- find the network interface on a Linux host without the ip command: the /proc/net/dev fallback took the file's header line for an interface, so such hosts, like slim Debian images, showed no network traffic; it now skips the two header lines ([c9fb7271](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/c9fb7271ec996657738feeadde3c7a0450e7379a))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.0...v0.7.1-beta.1](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.0...v0.7.1-beta.1)",
